preConditionHook:
// BROOKS'S ALWAYS-IN FLIP TEST: each of the last consecutiveBars bars is a
// STRONG bull trend bar -- a strict body direction, a body of at least
// bodyFraction of the bar's own range, and BOTH tails no more than tailFraction
// of it. Short is the mirror. "There usually has to have been at least two
// consecutive strong bull trend bars before most traders will believe that the
// always-in direction is long", hence consecutiveBars = 2.
//
// This is the RECOMMENDED DEFINITION behind the corpus's settled always-in
// decision, carried as its own rule so a placement can ask for the flip event
// directly; the rules that need the persistent DIRECTION still inline the state
// machine (TrendDurationBars, OutsideBarCounterTrend) rather than reference
// this file.
//
// NOT StrongTrendBarRun, which tests only the body on each bar of the run.
// Adding both tails is the same difference the catalog already draws between
// StrongTrendBar and CloseRangePosition: a shaved-top bull bar with a middling
// body passes one and fails the other. At tailFraction >= 1 the two rules do
// coincide; at the defaults they fire on different bars.
//
// NOT ConsecutiveUpBars, which tests only close against the bar's own open.
//
// The three tests cannot be ANDed in from other panes because they must hold on
// EACH bar of the run, not on the current bar.
//
// The all-of-N loop starts true and lets any failing bar clear the flag --
// StrongTrendBarRun's arrangement -- so the loop runs unconditionally and
// EasyLanguage's lack of short-circuiting cannot matter. The flags are class
// members and persist across bars, so both are reset at the top.
//
// Products, not quotients: EasyLanguage raises a runtime divide-by-zero and a
// zero-range bar is legal data.
//
// Deepest bar touched: consecutiveBars - 1.
allBull = true;
allBear = true;
for (int k = 0; k < (int)consecutiveBars; ++k) {
    rng = high[k] - low[k];
    if (el_le(close[k], open[k])) allBull = false;
    if (el_lt(close[k] - open[k], bodyFraction * rng)) allBull = false;
    if (el_gt(high[k] - close[k], tailFraction * rng)) allBull = false;
    if (el_gt(open[k] - low[k], tailFraction * rng)) allBull = false;
    if (el_ge(close[k], open[k])) allBear = false;
    if (el_lt(open[k] - close[k], bodyFraction * rng)) allBear = false;
    if (el_gt(close[k] - low[k], tailFraction * rng)) allBear = false;
    if (el_gt(high[k] - open[k], tailFraction * rng)) allBear = false;
}
